        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Manner: behaviour and body language"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 146.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Manners"
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 348.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Courtesy is still important nowadays. [politeness and respect]"
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 430.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The teacher said her students were always very courteous. [polite and respectful]"
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 466,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "She addressed the customer in a very discourteous manner. [impolite and lacking respect]"
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I hope I didn’t appear offhand with her – it’s just that I was in such a hurry. [showing a rude lack of"
      },
      {
        "y": 137.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 165.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "interest in others]"
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The boy had an insolent expression on his face which irritated me. [rude and not showing respect"
      },
      {
        "y": 161.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 232.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(much stronger than discourteous)]"
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "What’s the etiquette at a traditional Chinese wedding? Do you know? I’ve had an invitation to one."
      },
      {
        "y": 185.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 450.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[set of rules or customs for accepted behaviour in particular social groups or social situations]"
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 465.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Here, have a seat. Relax – there’s no need to stand on ceremony. [behave in a formal way]"
      },
      {
        "y": 208,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 474.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "My elderly uncle and aunt are both rather straitlaced. [having old-fashioned and fixed morals]"
      },
      {
        "y": 220,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Asking for more food at a formal dinner party is just not the done thing. [what you are expected to do in"
      },
      {
        "y": 233.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 165.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a social situation]"
      },
      {
        "y": 244,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "When taking part in online discussions, always follow netiquette and keep your comments brief."
      },
      {
        "y": 257.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 264,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[code of behaviour when using the internet]"
      },
      {
        "y": 280,
        "x0": 111.8,
        "x1": 206.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 304.3,
        "x0": 112.8,
        "x1": 486.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Manners, meaning the way we behave with one another socially, is plural, e.g. We need to employ"
      },
      {
        "y": 315.9,
        "x0": 112.8,
        "x1": 477.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "staff with good manners (NOT good manner). Manner (singular) is a more formal alternative to"
      },
      {
        "y": 327.9,
        "x0": 112.8,
        "x1": 394.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "‘way (of doing something)’, e.g. He greeted everyone in a friendly manner."
      },
      {
        "y": 362.1,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 320.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Body language and non-verbal language"
      },
      {
        "y": 380,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Research shows that we communicate more through body language and non-verbal noises than we"
      },
